WEBVTT

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:10.700
The Abh are not interested in the planets they conquer.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:17.990
That is because the Abh aim to dominate space and not the surface worlds that exist within space.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:22.410
What the Empire obtains from the surface worlds...

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:26.500
...are interplanetary trading rights and control of spaceships capable of planar space flight.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.190
It is an attempt...

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:36.030
...to prevent an otherwise inevitable interstellar war which would likely erupt among humankind.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:46.020
This is why the Abh are seen as possessing an arrogant and reckless nature.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:20.380
Carsarh Gerélacr

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:20.380
Kin of the Stars

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.120
Jinto! Hey!

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.600
Lynn Jinto!

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:04.500
Cu Dourin!

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.810
You look well.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.040
Thanks...

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.740
...for coming.

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:18.880
I'm the only one seeing you off.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.650
No one else is coming.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.220
Is that so?

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.890
Don't think badly of them.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.900
They're all just surprised.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:31.190
They knew you were going to an Abh school...

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:34.100
...but nobody knew your status.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:42.840
It's okay.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:47.280
It's my fault for keeping it a secret.

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:51.580
But would you have let me in your group...

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:53.590
...if you knew I was nobility?

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:55.880
No.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.720
We wouldn't have let you hang out with us if we knew...

00:03:58.790 --> 00:03:59.990
...what a lousy player you were.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.390
What do you mean?!

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.320
It's a first for everyone.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:09.530
Nobody knows how they should act around nobility.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:14.300
Neither do I.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.840
That outfit really suits you.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:21.480
Hey, stop kidding.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:23.550
Here you go.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:24.840
Thanks.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:25.910
Look.

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:30.690
That lady over there has the hots for you.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:32.190
I envy you.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:35.030
Older women have a thing for you!

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.060
Huh?

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:44.230
Man! If only I could have your face.

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:48.570
It's just unusual for a terran to be wearing an imperial uniform.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.200
It's like they're watching a dog use chopsticks.

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:53.140
A dog?

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.710
No, it's much more than that.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:59.920
Well, for a terran, that is.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.690
Guess so.

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:05.920
Hey...

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:10.550
I've only seen Abhs on holograms...

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:13.190
...but are they really all beautiful as they say?

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:14.360
I dunno.

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:16.930
I've never seen them in person myself.

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:20.430
<i>No.</i>

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:23.270
<i>He couldn't return</i> <i>even if he wanted to.</i>

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:26.780
<i>You can't expect the Empire to easily give him a title.</i>

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:29.250
<i>He's being tricked himself.</i>

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:30.880
<i>Serves him right!</i>

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:35.220
I know now how animals feel when they're taken to a zoo.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:38.590
I get here in the midst of confusion and...

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:44.490
...I'm off to the capital after just learning how to read and write.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:45.460
What?

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:47.630
Aren't you going home?

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:49.000
No.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:51.560
I'm going to officer training school.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:55.110
Are you going to join the military?

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:56.640
It's my duty.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:59.440
I have to serve in the Laburec for at least 10 years...

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:01.450
...before I can take the title.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:04.510
It's not easy being nobility, huh?

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:09.080
The higher your rank, the greater the duty.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.590
It makes more sense than the other way around.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:15.260
Does that mean you'll be going on warships?

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:16.160
Yeah.

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:19.130
In fact one is on its way to pick me up at 18 o'clock.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.090
What?!

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:23.540
A warship's entering this spaceport?

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.300
Why do you think I'm dressed like this?

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:28.810
So Abh soldiers will be coming here?

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:30.810
I don't know whether or not they'd be Abhs...

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:33.280
...but I know a military officer of the Laburec is coming.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:35.740
It's almost 18 o'clock.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:40.190
Is it? Then I should be leaving about now.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:44.720
Aren't you going to stay and watch me being escorted away?

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:46.360
I'd rather not.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:50.360
I might start crying from pity, seeing how miserable you look.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:51.900
Not likely.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:54.630
You're the cruelest villain in all of Delctuh.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:56.260
Don't speak so highly of me.

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:57.530
You're making me blush.

00:06:58.410 --> 00:06:59.840
By the way...

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:04.110
...what's the official name you use as a nobleman?

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:08.780
Linn Ssynec Rocr Ïarlucec Dreuc Haïder Ghintec.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:09.840
I think that's it.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:13.650
What do you mean you 'think'? It's your own name!

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:16.220
I'm still not used to it.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.350
Seems like someone else's name.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:22.020
Really.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:24.890
Okay, Ïarlucec Linn something Ghintec something.

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:27.870
Don't you forget my name, Cu Dourin.

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:33.130
It's a lot easier to remember than Linn something or rather Ghintec.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:34.540
I won't forget it.

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:37.200
You can ignore the formality...

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:39.980
...but don't you forget the name Lynn Jinto.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:41.270
All right.

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:45.150
Well, Linn Ssynec Rocr Ïarlucec Dreuc Haïder Ghintec.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:46.890
Here's a farewell present.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:49.950
Why, this is from...

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:53.320
A memento from Planet Delctuh.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:56.330
Are you going already?

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:57.460
Yeah.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:07:59.860
I can have this?

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:01.590
Yeah.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:05.600
<i>I hope you have a</i> <i>splendid trip in space.</i>

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:08.840
<i>Hope you get to travel with</i> <i>a beautiful cabin attendant.</i>

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:10.440
<i>Stop it.</i>

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:13.780
<i>I'd rather be with you than</i> <i>with any beautiful attendant.</i>

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:15.010
<i>Not me.</i>

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:16.680
<i>Hey, I'm trying to be sincere.</i>

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:18.720
<i>Then we'll continue</i> <i>this discussion next time.</i>

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.120
<i>Yes. Next time,</i> <i>when I return.</i>

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:24.690
<i>I'll even hire you at</i> <i>my company.</i>

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:25.950
<i>I'm counting on it.</i>

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:27.650
<i>I can boast that...</i>

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:31.060
<i>...our company employs</i> <i>a former imperial nobleman.</i>

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:32.290
<i>Sounds good.</i>

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:35.730
<i>Dourin,</i>

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:38.870
<i>Good-bye.</i>

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:42.970
<i>And so I watched...</i>

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:48.240
<i>...him go as he walked away,</i> <i>disappearing beyond the doors.</i>

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:52.180
<i>He never looked back.</i>

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:25.450
Blue hair?!

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:43.910
Excuse me!

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:28.440
Your Excellency Linn Ssynec Rocr Ïarlucec Dreuc Haïder Ghintec?

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:32.150
Why, yes I am.

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:36.210
Oh, but... first of all, thank you.

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:43.330
I've come from the patrol ship Gosroth to pick you up.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:45.060
You shall come with me.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:56.430
Just a minute.

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:58.600
<i>But, wait...</i>

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:02.040
<i>Wait a minute.</i>

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:05.910
<i>Wait...</i>

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:10.450
I asked you to wait!

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:16.560
You already know my name, right?

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:22.200
Aren't you Linn Ssynec Rocr Ïarlucec Dreuc Haïder Ghintec?

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:23.800
Yes.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:28.570
I am the Linn something or rather Ghintec as you say.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:34.640
I just feel, well, awkward that you know my name...

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:37.580
...but I don't know yours.

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:40.840
So, I was wondering...

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:44.860
Well, I don't know...

00:11:47.360 --> 00:11:49.130
...about the Abh, but...

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:53.600
You shall call me Lafiel!

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:58.830
<i>It was as if she were</i> <i>declaring victory in war.</i>

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:00.600
In exchange...

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:05.480
...I would like to refer to you only as Jinto.

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:08.250
Is that all right?

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:09.650
Ah, sure!

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:11.050
Of course it's all right!

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:13.350
In fact, I would prefer you call me that.

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:21.390
I forgot!

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:23.790
Oba-san!

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:26.990
Here's your bag.

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:41.710
Oba-san...

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:46.850
Jinto.

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:49.520
Let's go.

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:58.220
Trespassing Forbidden

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:58.220
Imperial Laburec Sector

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:01.470
Jinto.

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:02.500
Yes?

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:05.600
Earlier, when I saluted you...

00:13:05.670 --> 00:13:07.300
...you stepped back.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:08.270
Why was that?

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:10.640
Oh, that?

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:13.540
That's how we greet people on my home planet.

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:16.310
Very unusual.

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:19.790
It was like you were guarding against being hit or something.

00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:21.460
Really?

00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:25.790
Other cultures can seem strange to those not accustomed to it.

00:13:27.100 --> 00:13:29.260
But Jinto, you're an Abh...

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:33.390
...so you should get used to how the Kin of the Stars do things.

00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:37.760
Kin of the Stars...

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:41.300
<i>Known as the product</i> <i>of genetic art...</i>

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:43.640
<i>...they generally appear</i> <i>beautiful and ageless.</i>

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:46.680
<i>They live for over 200 years</i> <i>and have blue hair...</i>

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:50.540
<i>...and their bodies are</i> <i>built for life in space.</i>

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:52.650
<i>The Kin of the Stars...</i>

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:55.050
<i>Due to their affinity for the stars, that is the term...</i>

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:56.820
<i>...they prefer to use.</i>

00:13:57.560 --> 00:14:00.720
<i>I was only accepted as one of them through...</i>

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:03.030
<i>...a law passed by the Empire.</i>

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:15.270
So, this is the Gosroth?

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:18.240
Is that supposed to be a joke?

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:22.650
Please don't forget that this is all new to me.

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:25.950
This is the Calike, a shuttle attached to the Gosroth.

00:14:26.020 --> 00:14:27.920
It seats 50 people...

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:30.580
...although you're the only passenger today.

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:32.290
I'm quite honored.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:36.130
Then who's going to pilot it?

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:37.320
Oh, ah...

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:39.330
Now, will this be okay for you?

00:14:39.470 --> 00:14:40.230
What?!

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:42.130
Do you mean there are other ships too?

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:43.970
I'm asking if the co-pilot seat is okay...

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:46.970
...or if you prefer the cabin in the back.

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:50.300
Well, are there any beautiful cabin attendants?

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:54.550
There aren't any beautiful cabin attendants...

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:55.950
...but there's an elegant pilot.

00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:59.480
Well, obviously, I'll sit in the co-pilot seat.

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:08.060
Is it true that by connecting that to the ship...

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:10.890
...you can tell everything that's going on around the ship?

00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:12.200
Yes.

00:15:12.270 --> 00:15:15.860
This allows me to feel everything the ship feels.

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:25.310
Do you find the spatial sensor that interesting?

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:27.680
Well, sure.

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:31.150
Nobody on land has the ability to see what's behind them.

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:34.910
But, in my case, I was born with it.

00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:41.750
Can you read this? At this speed?

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:42.800
No, I can't.

00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:45.360
Then, what is it for?

00:15:45.430 --> 00:15:48.200
The logic crystal is inspecting the spaceship.

00:15:48.270 --> 00:15:49.430
If there are any irregularities...

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:51.560
...it's displayed in red and the scrolling stops.

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:53.040
Wow...

00:15:57.050 --> 00:16:01.000
It's hard to imagine you can pilot the spacecraft with that.

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:02.520
What do you mean?

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:03.610
Think about it.

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:08.380
It just seems impractical to pilot it just with your fingers.

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:10.860
Is there a better way?

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:12.050
Well...

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:14.390
...for one thing...

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:18.190
...what if you wanted to use your left hand to grab something.

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:19.630
Grab what?

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:22.430
Nothing in particular. I'm just saying.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:26.170
I forget about my left hand while I'm piloting.

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:28.300
Forget about it?

00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:33.210
There.

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:34.680
We're done.

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:36.180
Pretty simple.

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:37.520
Yes.

00:16:37.590 --> 00:16:41.020
That's because the logic crystal does a lot of the work.

00:16:41.090 --> 00:16:43.890
But what if the machine makes an error?

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:45.720
Humans make errors.

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:48.190
That's reassuring.

00:16:49.130 --> 00:16:51.220
You worry too much...

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:53.490
...judging from what you've been saying.

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:56.830
There is no way the machine would break down so easily.

00:16:58.810 --> 00:16:59.800
I suppose.

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:01.370
Control.

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:05.310
<i>Delctuh No. 1 spaceport</i> <i>traffic control.</i>

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:09.210
This is the Calike from patrol ship Gosroth.

00:17:09.280 --> 00:17:14.620
Military vessel register number 01-00-0937684.

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:17.260
Request depressurization of No. 2 military pier.

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:17.920
<i>Roger.</i>

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:21.330
<i>Commencing depressurization</i> <i>for Calike of Gosroth.</i>

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:27.970
Hey.

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:30.130
Can't we see what's happening outside?

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:31.460
Do you want to look outside?

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:35.000
Yeah. I've got no spatial sensors after all.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:36.300
I see.

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:37.570
All right then.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.310
<i>Depressurization complete.</i>

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:46.480
Request open bay doors to No. 2 military pier.

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:47.450
<i>Roger...</i>

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:49.390
<i>...Calike of Gosroth.</i>

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:00.030
Open bay doors confirmed.

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:01.330
Request permission to launch.

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:03.630
Permission to launch granted.

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:07.330
Calike of Gosroth, do you require an electromagnetic boost?

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:08.930
Negative.

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:11.210
We'll launch using low-heat propulsion.

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:12.250
<i>Roger.</i>

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:17.220
I doubt you can withstand an electromagnetic boost.

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:22.280
<i>Calike of Gosroth,</i> <i>we wish you a safe return.</i>

00:18:22.420 --> 00:18:25.820
<i>Delctuh No. 1 spaceport</i> <i>traffic control, out.</i>

00:18:26.390 --> 00:18:29.760
Thank you. Calike of Gosroth, out.

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:47.270
Launch.

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:07.360
We're flying.

00:19:07.940 --> 00:19:09.270
Of course we are.

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:12.570
Any Abh child can fly a ship like this.

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:14.400
I'm sure you're right...

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:16.810
...but you seem very young yourself.

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:19.040
Are you telling me that I'm like a child?

00:19:19.110 --> 00:19:20.510
Not at all!

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:24.110
It's just very difficult to figure out how old you people are.

00:19:24.190 --> 00:19:27.150
Besides, it's rude to ask a woman her age.

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:29.680
I understand now.

00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:31.750
Your guess is right.

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:33.850
I just turned sixteen recently.

00:19:33.930 --> 00:19:35.160
Sixteen?!

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:39.190
You're a year younger than me.

00:19:41.170 --> 00:19:42.070
What was that?!

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:44.800
We've entered a safe acceleration area.

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:46.800
Oh, is that all.

00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:48.500
Would you mind if we accelerated?

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:49.300
Go ahead.

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:52.280
How much longer will it take us?

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:55.980
It all depends on how much acceleration you can withstand.

00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:58.040
I'm a terran.

00:19:58.120 --> 00:20:00.640
If you can withstand it, well, so can I.

00:20:00.860 --> 00:20:02.760
In that case, we'll be there in under seven minutes.

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:03.690
Here we go!

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:10.290
Wh-What's going on?!

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:13.200
We're accelerating. You said you'd be okay.

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:15.340
I-I didn't expect this!

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:18.900
I'm not okay at all!

00:20:18.970 --> 00:20:20.670
Shall I slow it down a bit?

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:23.410
Yes! Please!

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:24.940
How can you withstand it?!

00:20:25.810 --> 00:20:29.180
Our ancestors' ships weren't equipped with gravity control...

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:30.600
...so, living in high speed, weightlessness...

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:31.680
Lafiel!

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:33.810
Hurry, please...

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:35.190
All right.

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:37.990
Oh, Jinto, I also have a question.

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:39.920
Wh-What?

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:42.820
What's so rude about asking a woman her age?

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:49.370
It was a strange beginning.

00:20:51.710 --> 00:20:54.300
The beginning of our journey.

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:08.210
( Mechanical Components )

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:13.880
( Evil )

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:11.730
( Destruction )

00:22:21.600 --> 00:22:23.620
( True identity of the Kin of the Stars )

00:24:35.630 --> 00:24:37.890
I am commander of the patrol ship Gosroth.

00:24:37.970 --> 00:24:39.260
I am Bomoüass Laicch.

00:24:43.940 --> 00:24:44.870
Ablïarsec?!

00:24:45.240 --> 00:24:47.230
I thought I told you earlier.

00:24:50.010 --> 00:24:51.140
Daïsairé!

00:24:52.410 --> 00:24:53.680
Tell me.

00:24:53.750 --> 00:24:56.180
Am I a daughter of love?

00:24:57.270 --> 00:25:00.030
Next episode

00:24:57.270 --> 00:25:00.030
Daughter of Love

00:24:57.270 --> 00:25:00.030
Frymec Négr
